| Layout / CSS / JS | `docs/_layouts/lexicum.html`, `assets/css/lexicum.css`, `assets/js/lexicum.js` | Yes |
| Receipt | `forge/receipts/LEXICUM-WEB.md` | No |

## Public surface rules

1. Show: field title, subfield schemes, concept `pref_label`, definition,
   alt labels, broader / narrower / related (human labels, not raw paths).
2. Provide client-side search + subfield filter; deep-linkable concept anchors.
3. One composition: brand (Creación Digital nav) + page title **Fashion Lexicum**
   as the route hero; one lede; then the catalogue. No dashboard card grid in the hero.
4. Follow existing site tokens (`site.css`); lexicum CSS is additive.
5. Standards line may mention SKOS / CIDOC-CRM; keep it one short sentence.
6. Publication firewall: fail if rendered HTML contains `Ahmes`, `Athanor`,
   `DevIAC`, `[BIBLIO-GAP]`, or absolute `/Users/` paths.

## Agent harness

1. Preflight: `cv/data/lexicum/MANIFEST.json` + `docs/_data/lexicum.json` exist and
   concept counts match.
2. Cold-review the forge contract before regenerating `docs/lexicum/index.md`.
3. After forge: Jekyll build (or liquid dry-check); spot-check `/lexicum/` for
   search, three schemes, and zero firewall leaks.
4. Write `forge/receipts/LEXICUM-WEB.md` with counts, sync timestamp, review verdict.

## Non-goals

- Do not auto-translate every label to Spanish in v1 (EN labels are the vocabulary
  spine; ES UI chrome is allowed).
- Do not invent concepts; only publish cloned snapshot terms.
- Do not turn the lexicum into a lesson with TTDO quotes or media slots.
